From e1b9a5a52372c7d2b1f8aec5997207a197be1588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:00:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(render): damage to the document element's subtree
 restyles the document without listing it

A retained restyle listed every damaged node in a set before cascading
them. A class change on <html> or <body> (Wikipedia's client preferences
flip several after load) damaged the whole document, and each such
mutation walked all 25,000 nodes again, with hash-set inserts per node,
before the cascade that re-styled them all anyway: about 0.6 s of
planning per forced layout. Damage now records the subtree roots it has
added, so a subtree inside one already added is not walked again, and
damage to the document element's subtree is planned as a whole-document
restyle (a fresh cascade, reported as a plan rather than a fallback).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
